hi everyone my name is Kathleen O'Toole  and I'm the assistant provost for k-12  education here at Hillsdale College I  thought I'd take a minute to talk to you  about the college's involvement in  kindergarten through 12th grade  education for decades the college has  been involved in the education of young  citizens first through Hillsdale Academy  a private school here on campus and in  the last ten years also through the  Barney charter school initiative which  is an outreach effort of the college  through the Barney charter school  initiative we support dozens of  classical charter schools all over the  country we helped found them we guide  them through the early stages of getting  school started and one school has begun  we provide comprehensive curriculum and  instruction advice to teachers our work  through the Barney charter school  initiative is made possible by numerous  friends of Hillsdale College in other  words the advice and support that we  provide our schools comes to those  schools absolutely for free we receive  nothing in return for the guidance and  advice that we give them except for the  satisfaction that they're doing an  excellent job one may ask why do we do  this why is it that for ten years the  college has been flying all over the  place helping these schools get started  well there are a number of reasons but I  think the first and most important is  that through these schools were seeing a  recovery of American public education  you know a couple of generations ago in  this country the education that was  possible in American public schools was  much more substantive much more serious  than it is today in other words the  education that students were receiving  in this country two or three generations  ago was much more substantive than the  education the average American public  school student receives today students  used to learn languages they used to  study math and a much more common  sensical and rigorous way they used to  diagram sentences they used to write in  cursive and on top of that they learned  about American history in a way that  made them understand and love our  country what we're seeing in these  charter schools and in Hillsdale Academy  itself here on campus is that the  ordinary American citizen the children  of those  are still capable of doing that  excellent work if only they're given the  opportunity and that's what the Barney  charter school initiative is all about
 

